The MIT license above covers tt's own code. tt also uses the software listed
below, each under its own license. Those licenses, not the one above, govern
that software.


Bundled in the tt binary or app
-------------------------------

libghostty-vt (Ghostty's terminal emulation core)
  https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty  (commit bd1c82bc, pinned in build.zig.zon)
  Copyright (c) 2024 Mitchell Hashimoto, Ghostty contributors
  License: MIT

uucode (Unicode data and grapheme breaking, used by libghostty-vt)
  https://github.com/jacobsandlund/uucode  (commit 9d555245)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Jacob Sandlund
  License: MIT
  Includes Unicode Character Database data, Copyright (c) Unicode, Inc.,
  under the Unicode License v3, and a UTF-8 decoder by Bjoern Hoehrmann
  under the MIT license.

Wuffs (pixel format conversion for Kitty graphics, used by libghostty-vt)
  https://github.com/google/wuffs  (commit 7411f488)
  Copyright 2023 The Wuffs Authors
  License: MIT or Apache License 2.0 (dual-licensed)

plotly.js v2.35.2 (interactive figures in notebook outputs)
  https://github.com/plotly/plotly.js
  Copyright 2012-2024, Plotly, Inc.
  License: MIT
  Vendored as assets/notebook/plotly.min.js. It bundles these packages,
  whose notices are in assets/notebook/plotly.min.js.LICENSE.txt:
    - polybooljs, (c) 2016 Sean Connelly: MIT
    - object-assign, (c) Sindre Sorhus: MIT
    - is-buffer, ieee754 and buffer, by Feross Aboukhadijeh: MIT
    - is-number and kind-of, (c) 2014-2015 Jon Schlinkert: MIT
    - maplibre-gl-js v4.5.2: BSD 3-Clause

Spline Sans
  https://github.com/SorkinType/SplineSans
  Copyright 2021 The Spline Sans Project Authors
  License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/OFL-SplineSans.txt)

Spline Sans Mono
  https://github.com/SorkinType/SplineSansMono
  Copyright 2022 The Spline Sans Mono Project Authors
  License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/OFL-SplineSansMono.txt)


Build toolchain (used to build tt, not shipped)
-----------------------------------------------

Zig 0.16 compiler and standard library
  https://ziglang.org  (Copyright (c) Zig contributors)
  License: MIT. Parts of the standard library are compiled into the binary.

translate-c (Zig's C translation package, fetched by Ghostty's build)
  https://github.com/ziglang/translate-c  (Copyright (c) Zig contributors)
  License: MIT

Aro (C compiler frontend, used by translate-c)
  https://github.com/Vexu/arocc  (Copyright (c) 2021 Veikka Tuominen)
  License: MIT; Unicode data under the Unicode License v3


System frameworks (part of macOS, linked but not shipped)
---------------------------------------------------------

Apple Foundation, AppKit, Metal, QuartzCore, CoreFoundation, CoreGraphics,
CoreText, ImageIO, WebKit, AVFoundation, UserNotifications and the
Objective-C runtime (libobjc). All are Copyright (c) Apple Inc. and are
covered by the macOS license terms.


Used at runtime if installed (not shipped with tt)
--------------------------------------------------

zsh: the shell tt runs, with assets/shell/tt.zsh for integration. MIT-like
  zsh license. https://www.zsh.org

Python, jupyter_client and ipykernel: the Python-side notebook kernel,
  started through assets/notebook/tt_jupyter.py. Python Software Foundation
  License (Python) and BSD 3-Clause (Jupyter). https://jupyter.org

Coding agents that "Fix with agent" can launch, each under its vendor's
  own terms: Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, GitHub Copilot CLI,
  Cursor Agent, Aider and Goose.

AI services the agent fallback can use, each under its provider's terms:
  Anthropic API, OpenAI API, Google Gemini API and a local Ollama server.
